            {
              "content": "= From the provided {{ $json.data }}, extract and present the following information in bullet points under the title \"Data Breach Snapshot\". Use the exact format shown below. \n  \nInstructions: \n  \nBold only the field titles. The values should remain un bolded. \n \nIf data is missing for a required field, follow the fallback instructions provided. Don't hallucinate, mention NA if you don't find any details. Perform a websearch wherever it is mentioned. \n  \nField Details to Extract: \n  \nEntity Name: Name of the organization that experienced the breach. \n  \nHeadquarters: City and State of the organization. Perform a web search if this information is not found in the data. Mention NA if cannot be searched \n \n# Impacted: Number of individuals/people or records impacted or exposed or affected. Mention the size of leak if available. If not specified, enter NA \n Date of Breach: Date of the breach, or incident or ransomware attack as reported. If not specified, enter NA \n \nDate Published; Date when the article was published \nInformation Compromised: List all the types of personal data (e.g., Names, SSN, DOB), separated by commas. Mention any type of information that was exposed or leaked. Mention NA if nothing is available \n \nLink to Where I Found Out About the Breach: Include the original source URL from the input data. \nExternal Source Link: Any other link that is mentioned in the article \nCompany URL: The official website of the breached entity. Search the web if not available in the input.  \nPresent the extracted data in this exact structured snapshot format: \n  \nData Breach Snapshot \n  \nEntity Name:  \nHeadquarters:  \n# Impacted:  \n Date of Breach: \nDate Published: \nInformation Compromised:  \nLink to Where I Found Out About the Breach:  \nExternal Source Link:  \nCompany URL: ",
              "role": "system"
            }
